Chapter: Game2048Wasm
  cites Games chapter Game2048
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for 2048, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Sixteen tiles that grow past a thousand each are
 well past an i32 packed together, so the page holds the state's address.

 `g2048-add-tile` writes the new tile with `list-set-at`, which mutates in
 place, so `g2-wasm-move` copies the grid before handing it to the engine.
 The engine has its own `g2048-copy-grid` and this chapter uses it rather
 than writing a second copier.

 A direction that changes nothing is not a move: `g2048-move` compares the
 slid grid against the old one and answers the state unchanged, so the page
 can tell a refused swipe from an accepted one by the handle coming back
 the same.

 We say:

Section: The Browser Interface

  g2-wasm-new : Integer -> G2048State
  g2-wasm-new (seed) = g2048-new (rng-new seed)

  g2-wasm-cell : G2048State, Integer -> Integer
  g2-wasm-cell (st) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= 16 then (-1)
    else list-at (st.grid) i

  g2-wasm-score : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-score (st) = st.score

  g2-wasm-moves : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-moves (st) = st.moves

  g2-wasm-done : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-done (st) = if st.game-over then 1 else 0

  g2-wasm-max : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-max (st) = g2048-max-tile (st.grid)

  g2-wasm-empty : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-empty (st) = g2048-empty-count (st.grid)

  g2-wasm-sum : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-sum (st) = g2048-sum-grid (st.grid)

  g2-wasm-can : G2048State, Integer -> Integer
  g2-wasm-can (st) (dir) =
    if dir < 0 then 0
    else if dir > 3 then 0
    else if st.game-over then 0
    else let after = g2048-apply-dir (g2048-copy-grid (st.grid)) dir
    in if g2048-grids-equal (st.grid) after then 0 else 1

  g2-wasm-move : G2048State, Integer -> G2048State
  g2-wasm-move (st) (dir) =
    if dir < 0 then st
    else if dir > 3 then st
    else if st.game-over then st
    else g2048-move (G2048State {
      grid = g2048-copy-grid (st.grid),
      score = st.score,
      moves = st.moves,
      game-over = st.game-over,
      rng = st.rng
    }) dir

  g2-wasm-ai : G2048State -> Integer
  g2-wasm-ai (st) =
    if st.game-over then (-1)
    else g2048-ai-dir st

